  "reason": "The current best result is config_038 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat) at 0.721 accuracy, which substantially outperforms the RNA-only multiprofile baseline (0.653). The image modality alone was weak (0.208 with resnet50), but the ViT-L encoder in the multimodal setting clearly adds value. The key remaining question within this winning configuration is whether the fusion strategy can be improved: concat treats both modalities equally, while weighted fusion could allow the model to adaptively downweight the weaker image signal and upweight the stronger RNA signal. Config_039 isolates exactly one variable (fusion: concat→weighted) from the current best, making it a clean exploitation experiment. With only 2 experiments remaining after this one, testing the most promising single modification to the current champion is the highest-value use of the next slot, and the result will directly inform whether the final 2 experiments should further refine this configuration or explore an alternative."
}

